{"content":[{"c":["PENUEL* (P",{"c":["lace"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Name given to the place near the Jabbok River where Jacob strove all night with God (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.32.31","r":"Gen.32.31","rawR":"Gen.32.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.32.31","value":"Gen.32.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 32:31"},"); alternately called Peniel in verse ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.32.30","r":"Gen.32.30","rawR":"Gen.32.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.32.30","value":"Gen.32.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"30"},". During the period of the judges, Gideon destroyed the tower of Penuel and killed the men of the city for refusing to join him in war against the Midianites (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.8.8-9,17","r":"Judg.8.8-9,17","rawR":"Judg.8.8-9,17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.8.8-9,17","value":"Judg.8.8-9,17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 8:8-9, 17"},"). Later, King Jeroboam rebuilt the town (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.12.25","r":"1Kgs.12.25","rawR":"1Kgs.12.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.12.25","value":"1Kgs.12.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 12:25"},"). It was positioned near Succoth east of the Jordan River, though its exact location remains uncertain."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"PenuelPlace","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 32:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.32.31","rawQueryValue":"Gen.32.31","sourceRefExact":"Gen.32.31"},{"anchorText":"30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.32.30","rawQueryValue":"Gen.32.30","sourceRefExact":"Gen.32.30"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 8:8-9, 17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.8.8-9,17","rawQueryValue":"Judg.8.8-9,17","sourceRefExact":"Judg.8.8-9,17"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 12:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.12.25","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.12.25","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.12.25"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b43b41836c432c3e0f932fd2a056ed88de8d2da051d6cd39afb23d638c49723f","sourceItemName":"PenuelPlace","sourceItemOrder":106,"sourceMember":"Articles/P.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"PenuelPlace","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Penuel* (Place)","title":"Penuel* (Place)","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}